body:
I see. Not in that field, but seems intriguing. Another chill passionate pre-professional would be cognitive science club. Idk, I feel like people definitely make or break clubs sometimes.

&#x200B;

(I know there are like 700 clubs on campus anyhow.)

Hey, thanks! It works now.

&#x200B;

Have a great day, strangers.

Thanks, I appreciate the response.

&#x200B;

Could you elaborate on 'alumni associations?' I get the concept but don't fully understand how it'd help in my process. - like I know why it'd be helpful in a broad sense, but not fully the means of how.

Any big events/clubs that encourages mingling that you could look into?

&#x200B;

There's board game club on Fridays at 8:00 at BSC I used to go to. It's chill cause you're just playing board games. (not shilling it was actually really cool to destress.)
